cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MorphIt in your research, please cite the MorphIt paper
  (preferred citation below). To refer to this Rust implementation, cite the
  software itself.
title: "MorphIt-rs: a Rust port of MorphIt"
abstract: >-
  Rust port of MorphIt: approximate a triangle mesh with a fixed budget of
  spheres by gradient-based optimization, with a thread-safe C API, a
  wgpu GPU backend, an HTTP server, WebAssembly bindings and an interactive
  studio.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kevin
    family-names: Gliewe
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KevinGliewe/MorphIt-rs"
url: "https://kevingliewe.github.io/MorphIt-rs/"
keywords:
  - sphere packing
  - collision geometry
  - robotics
  - mesh approximation
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "MorphIt: Flexible Spherical Approximation of Robot Morphology for Representation-driven Adaptation"
  authors:
